WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.280
- All right, let's close
out with something uplifting

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.201
I found on the web, this
is "What I'm liking".

00:00:04.201 --> 00:00:05.176
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.176 --> 00:00:07.050
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.720
Summer is almost here in
every part of this country,

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.460
there are some activities to try.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.110
Here in California you've got surfing

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.240
if you like wetsuits, which I don't.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.010
There are great mountain biking trails

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.050
in North Carolina, beautiful actually.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.300
And in Boston, there's rowing
as far as the eye can see

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.620
down the Charles River.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.453
So many things.

00:00:23.453 --> 00:00:25.650
And one Boston organization is working

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.360
to make sure rowing is accessible.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.570
Particularly to kids of all
backgrounds across the city

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.660
as well as para-athletes
and military vets.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.490
And this isn't just about exercise,

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.960
it's about peace of mind.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.660
To tell us more, let's say
hi to the executive director

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.290
of Community Rowing, Inc.,
Ted watching on NBC Boston.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.176
What's up Ted?

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:45.547
(audience applauds)

00:00:45.547 --> 00:00:47.823
- So nice to see you, Kelly, thank you.

00:00:47.823 --> 00:00:49.170
- Nice to have you on here, man.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.960
So your organization is reaching
a wide variety of people.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.820
So tell us about that.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.770
- Yeah, so a lot of people think rowing

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:00.270
is an elitist East coast activity
reserved just for the few.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:03.090
And community rowing
serves about 10,000 people

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:06.270
in our community, 85% of whom are youth.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.580
The other 15% are adults obviously.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.070
But we serve 40 public schools in the city

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.320
in collaboration with our partner schools.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.990
We go into schools and
bring rowing to kids.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.270
They also come out to our facility.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.920
We also serve veterans

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.200
and their families
through free programming.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.960
We go into VA hospitals as
well as bring those folks

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.930
back out to our place to
get on the Charles River.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.910
Like you said, we have programs for people

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:33.120
with intellectual and
physical disabilities as well.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.590
Partnership with Children's Hospital

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.200
for kids suffering from obesity.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.160
And then we provide affordable
programming and access

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.320
for people who wouldn't
otherwise have the background,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.990
experience or ability to
get on the Charles River.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.072
- That's incredible.

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:47.905
(audience applauds)

00:01:47.905 --> 00:01:51.240
Most people I would assume,
have not rowed before.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.070
I have, it's so peaceful, I love it.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:53.970
But most people haven't.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.210
So why do you think this
sport benefits people so much?

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.100
- So we've all seen the posters, right?

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.640
So you know, the teamwork
posters or the cliches

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.030
about putting all your
oars in the water together.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:07.800
One thing that's special about rowing

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.950
is that it's not only
talked about but it's felt.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.240
And with our military vets,

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.860
one of the things they say about rowing

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.280
is that they experience the
team concept while rowing.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.820
So they're getting a mental connection,

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.820
of physical benefits of being together.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.920
But you learn instantly,
whether you're putting the oars

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.420
in the water together or not.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.540
And part of the activity is to give people

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.480
healthy physical and
safe places to come out

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.040
and experience the growth that can come

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.887
from something as fun as
being on the river in the city

00:02:37.887 --> 00:02:39.930
and the parklands around our city.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:40.763
- Absolutely.

00:02:40.763 --> 00:02:41.910
That connection is so
important, especially

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.800
after so many years that
we were, 'cuz of COVID,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.510
everybody was isolated, right?

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.343
It's so important.

00:02:46.343 --> 00:02:48.801
But also I will say, rowing
alone is therapeutic as well.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.540
Just being out on the
water and it being still,

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.030
it takes a lot for some of us with ADHD

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.890
to just be still sometimes.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.530
And it's such a beautiful experience.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.520
Thank you so much Ted.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:00.570
What you're doing is so awesome.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.730
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:02.843
(audience applauds)

00:03:02.843 --> 00:03:03.960
- Oh, thank you very much Kelly.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.120
Yeah, that's so wonderful.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:05.953
Thank you.

00:03:05.953 --> 00:03:06.786
(audience applauds)

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:07.620
- All right, and that's not all.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.410
Our season-long partner
Pilot pen, makers of FriXion,

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.870
the go to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.390
want to celebrate those
helping break down barriers

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:17.550
and open up opportunities
just like you, my man.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.070
So they're gonna give
Community Rowing Inc.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:20.970
a thousand dollars.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:21.803
How's that sound?

00:03:21.803 --> 00:03:23.687
(audience applauds)

00:03:23.687 --> 00:03:24.990
- Thank you so much.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.130
- Absolutely, Ted.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.930
Keep doing the work, man, it's working.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.171
Thank you to all our
guests this hour as well.

00:03:30.171 --> 00:03:32.492
Garth Brooks, Gwen and Ezri

00:03:32.492 --> 00:03:35.670
Y'all have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

